# Every text file is LF in the repository and stays LF in a Windows checkout (#14). Windows
# runners and most Windows installs of git set core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites text files to
# CRLF on checkout. That broke byte-for-byte checks (the app runtime below is compared with what
# its source builds), test fixtures and snapshots, while nothing here needs CRLF. Every file in
# the index was already LF when this line was added, so it renormalises nothing.
* text=auto eol=lf

# 앱 템플릿의 런타임은 스크립트가 만든 생성물이다 (pnpm build:app-runtime) — 검토하지 않고 diff도 보이지 않는다.
# 손으로 고치지 않는다: 테스트(app-template.test.ts)와 번들 스크립트가 소스로 다시 만든 것과 바이트까지 대조한다.
packages/agent-host/app-template/runtime/** linguist-generated=true -diff

# The content manifest fixtures are hashed byte for byte by the Rust verifier and the Node writer
# (apps/desktop/content-verify/tests/writer.rs). One of them holds every byte value, CR LF included,
# so no line-ending conversion may touch them.
apps/desktop/content-verify/tests/fixtures/writer/** -text

# Node's SHASUMS256.txt, its detached signature and the release key that signed it: gpgv checks the
# signature over these exact bytes (tooling/node-pin.test.ts)
tooling/fixtures/node-pin/** -text
